        "met_days": 0,
        "type": "launch",
        "label": "Launch — Titan II",
        "description": "Vandenberg AFB, 1994-01-25. Clementine — joint US Department of Defense / NASA mission. Originally designed to test SDI (Strategic Defense Initiative) sensors against an asteroid, with the Moon as a calibration target. First US lunar mission after Apollo 17 (21 years)."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 9,
        "type": "tli_or_tmi",
        "label": "Trans-lunar injection",
        "description": "1994-02-03, after an eight-day checkout in low Earth orbit. The STAR 37FM solid motor sent Clementine into a phasing loop that passed Earth twice before reaching the Moon."
      },
