        "description": "Pre-LOI checkout phase."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 25.05,
        "type": "edl_or_oi",
        "label": "Lunar orbit insertion",
        "description": "1994-02-19. Captured into a 415 × 2,940 km polar orbit. Mapped the lunar surface at multiple wavelengths over 71 days — first global high-resolution multispectral lunar map. Bi-static radar experiment data was later interpreted (controversially) as evidence of water ice at the lunar south pole — a disputed hint that spurred later ice searches."
      }
